{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The Fundamental Paradigms", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 3, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when talking about the fundamental paradigms in software programming.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Give detailed and important information regarding to the history of language programming in different periods of time.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}]}, {"content": "enpe7n4le01ob03re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adjectives Ending In \"-al\"", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Adding a suffix to some verbs and nouns is a way to form adjectives. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are some latin-rooted nouns and verbs  that can become adjectives by adding the suffix <strong>\u2013al</strong>. See the following charts:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Nouns</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Adjectives</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"practice\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"practical\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"function\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"functional\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"element\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"elemental\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"structure\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"structural\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"fundament\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"fundamental\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verbs\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"add\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"additional\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"intent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"intentional\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"benefit\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"beneficial\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"converse\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"conversational\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"criticize\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"critical\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "When using these adjectives in a sentence, place them in the usual adjective positions. For example:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<i>Programming, nowadays, is more<strong> functional</strong> than in the past.</br><strong>Structural</strong> problems need to be solved carefully.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The first computer program was the Analytical Engine, it was designed by Charles Babbage who also introduced very functional and important computing concepts. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Then, Hernan Hollerith provided an input and output using a very practical method: punched cards. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Numerical calculations were based on decimal numbers, which it meant that logic were represented with both, number and words. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There is some information dated back in 1940 when computers were electrical and included limited speed and memory capacity.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Past Tense in Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <strong>the simple past tense</strong> form to talk about actions that started and finished in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When using the simple past tense, you can use time expressions to indicate when the action took place.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:</br> <i>I<strong> took</strong> the test about fundamental paradigms <strong>last June</strong>.</br>Michelle <strong>designed</strong> the logo in <strong>December 1999</strong>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Remember that the verbs in simple past tense can be<i> regular or irregular.</i> Regular verbs are the ones that end in \u2013<strong>ed</strong>, -<strong>ied</strong>  or \u2013<strong>d</strong>. On the other hand, irregular verbs are the ones that have different variations when used in the simple past.</br></br>  Examples:</br>  <i>My boss<strong> bought</strong> me a new computer.</br> In 1950, Germans <strong>invented</strong> a high-level programming language.</br></br></i>  When asking <strong>questions in simple the simple past tense</strong>, you use the auxiliary <strong>did</strong>. However, remember that the action verb keeps its base form. Check these examples:</br></br> \t<i><strong>Did</strong> you <strong>buy</strong> the balloons for the party? </br><strong>Did</strong> the Germans <strong>invent</strong> a high-level programming language?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Did you learn something about it back in school?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Did you find information about the first programming languages? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Did this period establish the fundamental paradigms for programming languages?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "stepping stone ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a situation that helps to approach an objective", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What we need to know is that these paradigms became the stepping stones for the current programming languages.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le01ob03aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "paradigm ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a model, a pattern ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For example, most of the language paradigms created in that time such as Speakeasy, Simula, Smalltalk, and Prolog are still in use. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le01ob03aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "punched card ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a card in which data can be coded by making holes", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Then, Hernan Hollerith provided an input and output using a very practical method: punched cards.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le01ob03aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": " flowering ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "growing, increasing ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The 60s and the 70s brought a major flowering in the field of programming languages.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le01ob03aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "decade ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a period of ten years", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This decade was considered a starting point where the first steps appeared for programming language.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le01ob03aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "current ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "present time  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: What we need to know is that these paradigms became the stepping stones for the current programming languages.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n4le01ob03aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Look for more information about fundamental paradigms in software programming. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a post with the main characteristics of fundamental paradigms in software programming", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share with your partners the post you created.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I look for more information about fundamental paradigms in software programming. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I create a post with the main characteristics of fundamental paradigms in software programming. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share with your partners the post you created.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"exercises": [{"questions": [], "template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can give important information related to the history of software programming and its evolution.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about the fundamental paradigms in software programming.", "type": "Learning Ou